      "title": "From Atoms to Universes: The Architecture of Everything in the Age of AI",
      "content_html": "<p>AI has become a consumer product faster than it has become a discipline. Each week brings new models and more information than anyone can absorb, and the easy response is uncritical consumption. Architecture needs a different strategy, built on criticism and method. <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/ai\">AI</a> is now acquiring spatial intelligence, the capacity to understand how physical space behaves, and architects can test a project against its environment while they design it. Used with judgment, AI can bring architects closer to nature and its complexity, and make them better builders. We simulate the world to learn how to inhabit it.</p>",
